    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A self-declared republic in former British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a>, which broke away from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a> on 18 May 1991.</li><li>It built peace through clan conferences and combines an elected president and parliament with a house of elders.</li><li>It has its own army, currency and passports and holds competitive elections, but recognition remains very limited.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In 1960 British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a> was independent for only five days, from 26 June to 1 July, before uniting with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a>; Somaliland’s claim rests on that brief statehood.</p></aside>
    </section>

